  "has_quantitative_results": true,
  "summary": "The paper proposes Systemic Quantum Score (SQS), an evolutionary search method for quantum kernel feature maps evaluated on a 4,763-loan credit-risk dataset. Using simulated 2–10 qubit circuits, the method achieves kernel fitness up to 0.998 and an AUC of 0.658 when trained on only 10% of the data, slightly outperforming classical SVC (0.638) and XGBoost (0.632) in that extreme low-data scenario, while XGBoost performs best on the full dataset.",
